  html:`<p>Use the <b>first conditional</b> for <b>real, possible</b> situations in the future.</p>${TBL(["If-clause","Result"],[["<b>If</b> + Present Simple","<b>will / won't</b> + infinitive"],["<b>If</b> I <b>save</b> enough,","I<b>'ll buy</b> a car."],["<b>If</b> you <b>don't pay</b> the bill,","they<b>'ll cut</b> the electricity."]])}<p style="margin-top:12px;"><b>unless</b> = if not: I won't buy it <b>unless</b> it's on sale.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;"><b>when / as soon as</b> = it <b>will</b> happen: I'll call you <b>as soon as</b> I <b>get</b> paid.</p><p style="margin-top:8px;">❗ No <b>will</b> after if / unless / when: ❌ If it will be cheap…</p>`,
